\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\ri-380\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 As they approached the research facility, two broad doors silently rolled open, granting access to a brightly lit atrium of marble and glass. Uncluttered by security gates, metal detectors or people, Dr\'92s Hardy and Jacobson quickly ambled across the gleaming marble towards the elevators. Dr Hardy pressed B10 and waited momentarily for an elevator to present itself and both climbed on board descended 100 metres below the ground to the test facility. 
\f1 \

\f0 The state of the art facility was where wild scientific theories clashed, sometime violently, with the laws of physics. Theoretical physicists could contrive any theory at a whim, but it fell to the experimental physicist to do the heavy lifting. 
\f1 \

\f0 Theoretically, it was expected that today\'92s test would form a stable stasis field, inside which time would slow almost, but not quite, to the point of cessation. Time could never stop moving forward, but it could be slowed down with a recipe of gravity waves, dark matter and dark energy. It all seemed so simple. 
\f1 \

\f0 \'93Boss?\'94 John ??? Said. \'93What music for today?\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \'93I think it\'92s Kathy\'92s call today, isn\'92t it\cf2 ? \cf0 Kathy?\'94 Dr Hardy asked.
\f1 \

\f0 \'93I have something very special.\'94 Kathy\'92s clear eyes sparkled brightly. \'93The Presley Brothers, Elvis and Jesse.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \'93Never heard of them\'94 Dr Hardy said.
\f1 \

\f0 \'93They were one of the first rock n\'92 roll gospel singers, about 100 years ago.\'94 She replied. \'93I can take or leave the songs, but theirs voice are spectacular.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \'91Okay, The Presley Brothers it is.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
